comments.body:
@jmanico sorry for the late reply, I agree with @randomstuff, extending V2.7 seems to be best for this. But [section 6](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-oauth-cross-device-security#name-mitigating-against-cross-de) lists many possible mitigations so I think it is hard to identify good ASVS verifications since it depends on the application and protocol.

Maybe something like this could be added?

> Verify that if cross-device solutions are used for authentication or delegating authorization then mitigations are in place to limit the risk of "device code phising". This includes e g  proximity checks (geolocation, network etc) and unique QR codes...
